{"id": "EUVD-2026-108844", "enisaUuid": "d5c3cbd1-fc86-3824-9834-94d0fb3f975c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: xilinx: fix runtime PM leak on request error path\n\npm_runtime_get_sync() leaves the usage counter incremented even when it\nfails, and xgpio_request() returns the error without dropping it.\n\ngpiolib does not call ->free() when ->request() fails, so xgpio_free(),\nwhich holds the only matching pm_runtime_put(), never runs. The reference\nis leaked and the controller can no longer runtime-suspend, so its clock\nstays enabled.\n\nSwitch to pm_runtime_resume_and_get(), which only increments the usage\ncounter on success.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b07b3925f676640103b3d74b93fc401b1c873d13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f73ee2bd2293f8cc340061c5229395ace71fc2eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a027e0d7765d1531ee39e4dae81951b04f32ba7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fd6ecda5d1f47cffcfadddb35ee49402162c724", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff82fc3a4a1d417dee1229681cc5285986edb1fa"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99049"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09aebc92-bb05-3878-be38-2f454062871d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "2ba457de-3c64-37d2-bb0a-76c786401294", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "26b04774621ed333e8bc56479feb6e31625df58c <ff82fc3a4a1d417dee1229681cc5285986edb1fa"}, {"id": "39e4c84a-8558-3d2f-bc0c-9746d69f7acb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "4971f667-3964-3d06-94f0-5f6b08ab2cd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "26b04774621ed333e8bc56479feb6e31625df58c <f73ee2bd2293f8cc340061c5229395ace71fc2eb"}, {"id": "5acb6c1c-007f-35b4-bf9d-f1f3c091191f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "62456337-a44e-3a25-bdc9-fb72669a6fed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "26b04774621ed333e8bc56479feb6e31625df58c <b07b3925f676640103b3d74b93fc401b1c873d13"}, {"id": "a0acd8bd-75d4-3ea0-82ef-4fc7b19f4695", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "26b04774621ed333e8bc56479feb6e31625df58c <2fd6ecda5d1f47cffcfadddb35ee49402162c724"}, {"id": "ad24902f-7dd7-35be-aa92-d1d60f61cc26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "26b04774621ed333e8bc56479feb6e31625df58c <a027e0d7765d1531ee39e4dae81951b04f32ba7b"}, {"id": "b8401913-0278-3c3c-bbc5-3b45f53c3c3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b974343f-2c0c-3dd9-aab3-6c39f2486638", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "bf0cec2f-64b3-3f94-9515-34240df6b5ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f193c68e-782f-3003-827a-b4e13440bf7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e20187f8-66cd-334c-a359-a06cd5230f9e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}